<table class="wal-observations" role="table">
 <caption>Observations that answer different WAL questions in PostgreSQL 18</caption>
 <thead role="rowgroup"><tr role="row"><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Question</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Useful observation</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Interpretation</th></tr></thead>
 <tbody role="rowgroup">
  <tr role="row"><th scope="row" role="rowheader">How much log is generated?</th><td role="cell"><span class="cell-label" aria-hidden="true">Useful observation</span><code>pg_stat_wal</code>: <code>wal_bytes</code>, <code>wal_records</code>, <code>wal_fpi</code></td><td role="cell"><span class="cell-label" aria-hidden="true">Interpretation</span>Take deltas over a known interval. Full-page images help explain a change after checkpoint activity.</td></tr>
  <tr role="row"><th scope="row" role="rowheader">Why did checkpoints run?</th><td role="cell"><span class="cell-label" aria-hidden="true">Useful observation</span><code>pg_stat_checkpointer</code>: timed and requested counts; checkpoint log messages</td><td role="cell"><span class="cell-label" aria-hidden="true">Interpretation</span>Repeated size-driven requests may justify more WAL allowance. A manual checkpoint is also requested work.</td></tr>
  <tr role="row"><th scope="row" role="rowheader">Where did checkpoint time go?</th><td role="cell"><span class="cell-label" aria-hidden="true">Useful observation</span>Checkpoint log: write, sync and total; checkpointer write and sync totals</td><td role="cell"><span class="cell-label" aria-hidden="true">Interpretation</span>Elapsed write time includes pacing. It is not all time spent actively writing bytes.</td></tr>
  <tr role="row"><th scope="row" role="rowheader">Who wrote data buffers?</th><td role="cell"><span class="cell-label" aria-hidden="true">Useful observation</span><code>pg_stat_checkpointer</code>, <code>pg_stat_bgwriter</code>, <code>pg_stat_io</code></td><td role="cell"><span class="cell-label" aria-hidden="true">Interpretation</span>Checkpointer, background writer and client-backend work are distinct. A client needing a dirty buffer can pay its own write.</td></tr>
 </tbody>
</table>
<style>
.wal-observations{display:table;width:100%;table-layout:fixed;font:.9rem/1.6 var(--font-sans);overflow:visible;margin:1.5rem 0}.wal-observations caption{text-align:left;margin-bottom:.7rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.wal-observations th,.wal-observations td{padding:.65rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.wal-observations th:first-child{width:24%}.wal-observations th:nth-child(2){width:32%}.cell-label{display:none}
@media(max-width:600px){.wal-observations{display:block;font-size:.9rem;table-layout:auto}.wal-observations caption{display:block}.wal-observations thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip-path:inset(50%);white-space:nowrap}.wal-observations tbody,.wal-observations tr,.wal-observations th,.wal-observations td{display:block;width:auto}.wal-observations tr{padding:.8rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong)}.wal-observations th:first-child{width:auto;font-size:1rem;padding:.3rem 0 .6rem}.wal-observations td{padding:.3rem 0 .6rem;border:0}.wal-observations th{border:0}.cell-label{display:block;font-size:.8rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-bottom:.2rem}}
</style>
